// Each row has a distinct objective, teaching point, example, practice and check question.
const rows = [
 ['How websites work','Identify the job of each web language.','A browser reads HTML for structure, CSS for appearance, and JavaScript for behavior. These parts work together, but each solves a different problem.','<h1>Hello, web!</h1>','Choose the language for a heading, a color, and a click response.','Which language gives a page its structure?','HTML','CSS','JavaScript'],
 ['Files, folders, and paths','Link files with a correct relative path.','A relative path starts from the file that contains the link. An absolute URL starts with a scheme such as https://. Keep related files in clear folders.','<img src="images/cat.jpg" alt="A cat">','Fix a broken image path when the image lives in an images folder.','Where does a relative path start?','The current file','The web server root','The desktop'],
 ['Browser tools and first edits','Inspect a page and understand temporary edits.','Developer tools reveal the elements, styles, and console messages behind a page. Changes there help you experiment, but they do not update your saved source file.','<p id="message">Inspect me</p>','Inspect the paragraph and change its text temporarily.','Where should a permanent edit be made?','In the source file','Only in developer tools','In the address bar'],
 ['Document structure','Build the required parts of an HTML document.','The doctype tells browsers to use modern HTML. The head stores metadata such as the title; the body holds visible content.','<!doctype html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head><title>My page</title></head>\n<body><h1>Hello</h1></body>\n</html>','Add a title and visible heading to a basic document.','Where does visible page content belong?','The body','The head','The doctype'],
 ['Elements and attributes','Repair nesting and add attributes.','Most elements have opening and closing tags. Attributes add information inside the opening tag. Void elements, such as img, do not wrap content.','<a href="https://example.com">Example</a>','Repair malformed tags and add a useful link destination.','Where is an attribute written?','In the opening tag','After the closing tag','Only in CSS'],
 ['Headings and paragraphs','Write a clear introduction with a useful heading hierarchy.','A heading names a section. Use one main heading for the page, then lower levels for sections. Paragraphs hold related sentences; strong marks important meaning.','<h1>My learning page</h1>\n<p>I am learning to build websites.</p>\n<h2>My interests</h2>\n<p>I enjoy art and science.</p>','Add one main heading, an introduction paragraph, an interests heading, and a paragraph about your interests.','Which heading introduces a subsection below the page title?','h2','h1','p'],
 ['Lists and links','Create a list and descriptive section link.','Use ul for an unordered group and ol when order matters. Link text should describe its destination. A # link points to an id on the same page.','<a href="#goals">My goals</a>\n<h2 id="goals">My goals</h2>\n<ul><li>Practice HTML</li></ul>','List two interests and link to the list section.','Which list element shows steps in order?','ol','ul','li'],
 ['Images and alternative text','Add an image with appropriate alternative text.','The src locates the image. Alt text describes informative images for people who cannot see them; decorative images can use an empty alt.','<img src="photo.jpg" alt="Student sketching at a desk">','Add an informative image and describe what matters in it.','What does alt text provide?','A text alternative','A file path','A visual border'],
 ['Semantic page sections','Choose page elements by meaning.','Semantic elements describe the role of content. Put primary content in main, navigation in nav, and the page ending in footer.','<header><nav><a href="#main">Read</a></nav></header>\n<main id="main"><article><h1>News</h1></article></main>','Organize a small page using header, main, and footer.','Which element holds the primary content?','main','footer','nav'],
 ['Tables for data','Build a simple schedule table.','Tables represent data with rows and columns. Use th for headers and a caption to name the table; do not use tables merely to position a page.','<table><caption>Study plan</caption><tr><th>Day</th><th>Topic</th></tr><tr><td>Mon</td><td>HTML</td></tr></table>','Create a two-day study schedule with headers.','What is a table caption for?','Naming the data table','Sending a form','Styling a card'],
 ['Inputs, labels, and buttons','Build a labeled practice form.','A label names its control and can connect with for and id. Give buttons a clear type. HTML forms do not send messages without a delivery service.','<form><label for="name">Name</label><input id="name"><button type="submit">Practice</button></form>','Add a labeled name field and a practice submit button.','What connects a label to an input?','Matching for and id','Matching classes','A placeholder'],
 ['Form grouping and validation','Group controls and apply browser validation.','Fieldset and legend name a related group. Required and type attributes provide useful built-in checks, but important feedback still needs to be clear.','<fieldset><legend>Contact</legend><label>Email <input type="email" required></label></fieldset>','Group an email field and make it required.','Which element names a fieldset?','legend','label','summary'],
 ['Stylesheets and selectors','Connect a stylesheet and target a class.','A link element connects an external stylesheet. Class selectors start with a dot and can style many elements. Style a copy of your HTML project.','<p class="note">Practice daily</p>','.note { color: royalblue; }','Style a note using a class selector.','Which selector targets class="note"?','.note','#note','note()'],
 ['Cascade, inheritance, and specificity','Explain why a CSS rule wins.','Later rules can win when selectors have equal weight. More specific selectors can override general rules. Repeated !important makes future changes harder.','<p class="note">Hello</p>','p { color: gray; }\n.note { color: blue; }','Make the note blue and explain which selector wins.','Which selector is more specific?','.note','p','*'],
 ['Colors, units, and typography','Set readable type with relative units.','rem follows the root text size; em follows the element context. Use sufficient line height and a font stack so text remains readable.','<p class="intro">Read comfortably.</p>','.intro { font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.6; color: #253047; }','Style readable introduction text.','Which unit follows the root font size?','rem','px','vw'],
 ['The box model','Distinguish padding, border, and margin.','Padding sits inside the border; margin sits outside it. Border-box makes declared width include padding and border.','<div class="box">Content</div>','.box { padding: 16px; border: 2px solid; margin: 12px; box-sizing: border-box; }','Add internal and external spacing to a box.','Which property adds space outside a border?','margin','padding','line-height'],
 ['Backgrounds and decoration','Style a surface without obscuring text.','Background, border, radius, and shadow can group content. Keep decoration subtle and preserve readable contrast.','<div class="card">A useful card</div>','.card { background: #eef3ff; border: 1px solid #ccd; border-radius: 8px; }','Give a card a clear surface and border.','Which property rounds corners?','border-radius','box-sizing','outline'],
 ['Sizing, overflow, and display','Constrain width and manage long content.','Block elements begin a new line; inline elements flow with text. max-width prevents an element growing too wide, and overflow controls excess content.','<div class="box">Long content can wrap.</div>','.box { max-width: 40rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }','Keep a long text box inside a narrow view.','Which property caps an element’s width?','max-width','min-height','display'],
 ['Flexbox','Align flexible items with gaps.','Normal document flow stacks blocks. Flexbox makes one-dimensional rows or columns with gap, alignment, and wrapping.','<nav><a href="#a">A</a><a href="#b">B</a></nav>','nav { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }','Arrange navigation links with a gap and wrapping.','Which declaration enables Flexbox?','display: flex','position: fixed','float: flex'],
 ['Grid','Make responsive columns with flexible tracks.','Grid lays out rows and columns. minmax and repeat can create columns that adapt while respecting a useful minimum width.','<div class="grid"><div>A</div><div>B</div></div>','.grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 1rem; }','Build a two-column card grid.','Which property defines grid columns?','grid-template-columns','flex-direction','position'],
 ['Positioning and stacking','Use positioning only where it adds meaning.','Positioned elements can move relative to normal flow. Sticky stays in flow until scrolling reaches its threshold; z-index controls overlapping positioned layers.','<p class="badge">New</p>','.badge { position: sticky; top: 0; }','Make a small heading stick at the top while scrolling.','Which position mode sticks during scrolling?','sticky','static','inherit'],
 ['Flexible layouts and media queries','Adapt a layout at a content-driven breakpoint.','Start with a narrow layout, then add columns when space allows. Images should stay within their container.','<img src="photo.jpg" alt="A workspace">','img { max-width: 100%; }\n@media (min-width: 48rem) { main { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }','Make a layout switch to two columns on wide screens.','What does a media query test?','A viewing condition','A form value','A file extension'],
 ['Interaction states','Make focus and disabled states visible.','Hover helps pointer users; focus-visible serves keyboard users. Disabled controls should be understandable without relying on color alone.','<button>Save</button>','button:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid royalblue; }','Add a visible keyboard focus style to a button.','Which state helps keyboard navigation?','focus-visible','hover only','visited'],
 ['Transitions and animation','Add motion while honoring reduced-motion preference.','Transitions animate between values. Keep motion subtle and turn it off when a learner requests reduced motion.','<button>Open</button>','button { transition: background .2s; }\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { button { transition: none; } }','Create a short hover transition and reduced-motion override.','What preference can request less animation?','prefers-reduced-motion','max-width','color-scheme'],
 ['Variables and data types','Store values using const and let.','Use const when a binding will not be reassigned and let when it will. JavaScript values include strings, numbers, booleans, null, and undefined.','<p id="out"></p>','','const topic = "HTML";\ndocument.querySelector("#out").textContent = topic;','Store a course topic and display it.','Which declaration permits reassignment?','let','const','typeof'],
 ['Operators and comparisons','Compare values without surprising coercion.','Arithmetic combines numbers. Strict equality compares type and value. Logical operators combine conditions.','<p id="out"></p>','','document.querySelector("#out").textContent = 2 + 3 === 5;','Compare two scores and show the result.','Which operator checks strict equality?','===','==','=','<>'],
 ['Strings and template literals','Build a message from values.','Template literals use backticks and ${} placeholders. String methods such as trim help clean user input.','<p id="out"></p>','','const name = "Sam";\ndocument.querySelector("#out").textContent = `Hello, ${name}`;','Create a greeting with a template literal.','Which syntax inserts a value in a template literal?','${value}','{value}','$(value)'],
 ['Conditions','Choose a branch using if and else.','An if block runs when its condition is truthy. Use else for the other case and explicit comparisons when possible.','<p id="out"></p>','','const ready = true;\ndocument.querySelector("#out").textContent = ready ? "Go" : "Wait";','Show a different message for ready and not ready.','Which block runs if an if condition is false?','else','if','return'],
 ['Functions and scope','Return a result from a function.','Parameters carry inputs into a function. return gives the caller a result; console.log only prints a message. Local variables stay inside the function.','<p id="out"></p>','','function double(n) { return n * 2; }\ndocument.querySelector("#out").textContent = double(4);','Write a function that adds one to a number.','Which keyword gives a result to the caller?','return','console.log','let'],
 ['Loops','Repeat work with a stopping condition.','A for loop has a start, condition, and update. A while loop needs a condition that eventually becomes false. for...of visits array values.','<p id="out"></p>','','let total = 0;\nfor (let n = 1; n <= 3; n++) total += n;\ndocument.querySelector("#out").textContent = total;','Sum the numbers from 1 through 5.','What prevents a loop from running forever?','A reachable stopping condition','A console message','A CSS rule'],
 ['Arrays','Store and iterate a list.','Arrays keep values in order. Indexes start at zero, length counts items, and push adds a value to the end.','<p id="out"></p>','','const tasks = ["Read", "Practice"];\ntasks.push("Review");\ndocument.querySelector("#out").textContent = tasks.length;','Add a school task and display the count.','What is the first array index?','0','1','-1'],
 ['Objects','Group named properties.','Objects pair property names with values. An array of task objects can store title and completed status for each task.','<p id="out"></p>','','const task = { title: "Read", done: false };\ndocument.querySelector("#out").textContent = task.title;','Create a task object and display its title.','How do you read the title property?','task.title','task[0]','title.task'],
 ['Array methods','Transform and filter a task list.','map creates a new array of results; filter keeps matching entries; find returns the first match; forEach visits each item.','<p id="out"></p>','','const tasks = [{title:"Read",done:true},{title:"Write",done:false}];\ndocument.querySelector("#out").textContent = tasks.filter(t => !t.done).length;','Filter unfinished school tasks.','Which method keeps matching items?','filter','push','length'],
 ['Selecting and updating elements','Update DOM text safely.','querySelector finds an element. Set textContent for learner-entered text so it appears as text rather than being interpreted as HTML.','<p id="out">Old</p>','','document.querySelector("#out").textContent = "New";','Select a paragraph and change its text.','Which property safely inserts user text?','textContent','innerHTML','outerHTML'],
 ['Events and event objects','Respond to a click.','addEventListener attaches behavior. The event object describes what happened; preventDefault stops a form submission when handling it in JavaScript.','<button id="go">Go</button><p id="out"></p>','','document.querySelector("#go").addEventListener("click", () => { document.querySelector("#out").textContent = "Clicked"; });','Make a button update a message.','Which method attaches an event handler?','addEventListener','querySelectorAll','preventDefault'],
 ['Creating and removing elements','Build a node without parsing user HTML.','createElement makes an element, append adds it, and remove deletes it. Set textContent for user input.','<ul id="list"></ul>','','const li = document.createElement("li"); li.textContent = "Study"; document.querySelector("#list").append(li);','Add a list item when a button is clicked.','Which method creates a new element?','createElement','createText','querySelector'],
 ['Custom form validation','Show field-specific errors.','Read and trim the field value, then explain the problem beside that field. Keep entered data so the learner can repair it.','<label>Task <input id="task"></label><p id="error"></p>','','const value = document.querySelector("#task").value.trim(); document.querySelector("#error").textContent = value ? "" : "Enter a task";','Reject a whitespace-only task title.','Which method removes surrounding whitespace?','trim','split','replaceAll'],
 ['JSON and local storage','Serialize and restore practice data.','localStorage stores strings in the preview browser. JSON.stringify converts data to text, and JSON.parse restores it. This exercise storage is separate from WebSteps progress.','<p id="out"></p>','','localStorage.setItem("study", JSON.stringify({day:"Monday"})); document.querySelector("#out").textContent = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("study")).day;','Save a task list as JSON and restore it.','Which method converts an object to JSON text?','JSON.stringify','JSON.parse','String.parse'],
 ['Errors and invalid saved data','Recover from damaged JSON.','Parsing can throw if saved text is damaged. Use try...catch, check the restored shape, and fall back to safe defaults.','<p id="out"></p>','','let tasks; try { tasks = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("tasks")); if (!Array.isArray(tasks)) throw Error("Invalid list"); } catch { tasks = []; } document.querySelector("#out").textContent = tasks.length;','Handle broken saved task data without crashing.','Which block handles a thrown parsing error?','catch','finally','if'],
 ['Promises and asynchronous behavior','Describe when a promise settles.','A promise represents work that may finish later. It can resolve with a value or reject with an error; code after scheduling can run first.','<p id="out">Waiting</p>','','Promise.resolve("Done").then(value => { document.querySelector("#out").textContent = value; });','Show a message after delayed work completes.','Which promise state means success?','fulfilled','rejected','pending'],
 ['Fetch and async/await','Load bundled JSON and handle HTTP failure.','fetch returns a response even for HTTP errors, so check response.ok. await pauses the async function until a promise settles.','<p id="out">Loading</p>','','async function load() { try { const r = await fetch("./sample-data.json"); if (!r.ok) throw Error(`HTTP ${r.status}`); const data = await r.json(); document.querySelector("#out").textContent = data.title; } catch(e) { document.querySelector("#out").textContent = e.message; } } load();','Load bundled data and show a friendly error on failure.','What should you check after fetch resolves?','response.ok','response.length','window.ready'],
 ['Loading, empty, and error states','Give useful feedback for every outcome.','Show loading while work is pending, an empty message when data has no items, and a retry action after failure. Restore disabled controls in every outcome.','<button id="retry">Load</button><p id="out"></p>','','document.querySelector("#retry").addEventListener("click", () => { document.querySelector("#out").textContent = "Loading…"; setTimeout(() => { document.querySelector("#out").textContent = "No tasks yet"; }, 400); });','Create loading, empty, and error messages for a task list.','What should an error state offer?','A useful retry action','A blank screen','A silent failure'],
 ['Debugging with browser tools','Trace a broken page using browser tools.','Read the first console error, inspect the element involved, and check the Network panel for failed files. Change one cause at a time, then rerun.','<p id="out">Inspect this</p>','','document.querySelector("#out").textContent = "Fixed";','Find and fix a misspelled selector.','Where do JavaScript exceptions appear?','The console','The address bar','The CSS file'],
 ['Keyboard and accessibility checks','Check labels, focus, and feedback.','Use Tab to reach every control, make focus visible, connect labels, and announce important results. Automated checks cannot judge every accessibility need.','<label for="name">Name</label><input id="name">','input:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid blue; }','Repair an unlabeled field and test it with a keyboard.','What should a visible label identify?','Its control','The browser tab','The stylesheet'],
 ['Responsive testing and refactoring','Test narrow layouts and simplify repeated code.','Resize through several content-driven widths, check long text and 200% zoom, and move repeated logic into clear functions.','<main><h1>Responsive page</h1></main>','main { max-width: 70rem; margin: auto; padding: 1rem; }','Fix horizontal overflow in a narrow page.','What should you test besides screen width?','Enlarged text and long content','Only desktop screenshots','Only colors'],
 ['Plan a personal portfolio','Turn a goal into sections and acceptance criteria.','List the content, navigation, theme behavior, and data-driven section before coding. Acceptance criteria say what must work when finished.','<h1>My portfolio plan</h1><ul><li>About</li><li>Projects</li></ul>','Write a plan with sections and testable criteria.','What is an acceptance criterion?','A testable outcome','A color palette only','A file name'],
 ['Integrate and test','Combine HTML, CSS, and JavaScript deliberately.','Build the page structure first, style across screen sizes, then add interactions. Test keyboard use and errors after every integration step.','<button id="theme">Change theme</button>','body.dark { background: #111; color: #fff; }','document.querySelector("#theme").addEventListener("click", () => document.body.classList.toggle("dark"));','Add a working theme control to a portfolio.','What verifies a button works?','Use it and observe the intended result','Its label alone','Its color'],
 ['Publish and verify','Check a published site as a visitor.','Deployment puts files on a host. Verify the live URL, direct paths, images, links, mobile layout, and browser console. A working local preview is not proof the live site works.','<a href="./projects.html">Projects</a>','Write a release checklist and verify each item after publishing.','Which path needs a direct-load check?','A lesson or detail URL','Only the home URL','Only a local file']
];

